    "content": "On September 4, 2026, Somali National Army special forces, known as Danab Commandos, conducted a planned operation in Buula-Fulaay, a locality in the Bay region of southwestern Somalia. The operation resulted in the deaths of 14 Al-Shabaab militants, according to a statement released by the military. Among those killed were five commanders and nine guards accompanying them.\n\nThe deceased commanders included Bishaar Mohamed Muqtaar, also known as Sheikh Bishaar, who was allegedly responsible for Al-Shabaab's activities in the Gedo region. Sheikh Bishaar had previously operated in the Bay and Lower Shabelle regions. The operation is part of ongoing efforts by Somali forces to degrade the militant group's presence in central and southern Somalia.\n\nThe Bay region has seen frequent military activity as government forces, supported by local militias and international partners, seek to reclaim rural areas from Al-Shabaab control. The group continues to launch attacks and impose taxes on local populations despite territorial losses. This strike is one of several recent targeted killings of mid-level Al-Shabaab leaders, which are intended to disrupt the group's command and control.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development underscores the continuing security challenges in their homeland but also highlights the progress made by Somali security forces in conducting precise operations. The Danab Commandos, trained by international partners, represent a growing capability within the Somali military. Diaspora communities often closely follow such operations, as they impact the safety of relatives and future investment prospects in the country. The stability of regions like Bay is crucial for the return of displaced families and the revival of agriculture, a key source of livelihood.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/06/kumaandooska-danab-oo-14-xubnood-oo-ka-tirsanaa-al-shabaab-ku-dilay-howlgal-ka-dhacay-gobolka-bay/",
